          <h1>Know what your agents actually did.</h1>
          <p class="landing-lede">
            Claude Code, Codex, pi, Cursor, and Grok leave a transcript on every machine they
            run on. akari is a self-hosted instrument that collects those
            sessions into one searchable history: every run readable end to end,
            every token priced, every project's spend on one screen.
          </p>
          <div class="landing-cta">
            <a class="btn" href="/guide">Read the guide</a>
            <a
              class="btn secondary"
              href="https://github.com/jssblck/akari"
              rel="noopener"
              target="_blank"
              >View on GitHub</a
            >
          </div>
          <!-- The hero demo: a framed session fragment, the way a developer-tool
				     landing leads with a real surface rather than a screenshot. -->
          <div class="landing-hero-demo">
            <div class="mock-frame">
              <div class="mock-bar">
                <span class="mock-crumb"
                  >jssblck/akari <span class="sep">/</span> session</span
                >
                <span class="spacer"></span>
                <span class="tag agent">claude</span>
                <span class="tag mk-grade mk-grade-b">B</span>
              </div>
              <div class="mock-body">
                <div class="mk-msg mk-msg-user">
                  <span class="mk-role">User</span>
                  <p class="mk-text">
                    the tests in internal/store are flaky under -race, find out
                    why
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div class="mk-msg mk-msg-assistant">
                  <span class="mk-role">Assistant</span>
                  <p class="mk-text">
                    Reproducing under -race, then bisecting the shared state.
                  </p>
                  <div class="mk-tools">
                    <span class="mk-chip"
                      ><span class="mk-tn">Read</span>
                      <span class="mk-file">internal/store/store_test.go</span>
                      <span class="mk-stamp">out: 4.2 KB</span>
                      <span class="mk-st ok">ok</span></span
                    >
                    <span class="mk-chip"
                      ><span class="mk-tn">Bash</span>
                      <span class="mk-file"
                        >go test -race -count=20 ./internal/store</span
                      >
                      <span class="mk-stamp">out: 1.8 KB</span>
                      <span class="mk-st err">err</span></span
                    >
                    <span class="mk-chip"
                      ><span class="mk-tn">Edit</span>
                      <span class="mk-file">internal/store/pool.go</span>
                      <span class="mk-stamp">in: 612 B diff</span>
                      <span class="mk-st ok">ok</span></span
                    >
                  </div>
                  <p class="mk-text mk-text-final">
                    The pool test shares a fixture across parallel runs; pinned
                    it per test.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="landing-caption muted">
              A session as akari shows it, from the prompt to the fix.
            </p>
          </div>
